promptListN [SimTalk]
Enables the user to pick one or several entries from the designated list, which is displayed in the message
window.
Remarks
The dialog, which the function opens is modal. The simulation only continues when the user reacted to
the requested interaction by clicking the respective button in the dialog.
The user can select one or several entries by Shift/Ctrl+clicking the objects and click OK.
Type
Function
Syntax
promptListN(List:list[, Text:string, ...]) → list
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter List of data type list designates the list.
promptListN [SimTalk]
12-568 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The user can select one or more entries by holding down Ctrl and clicking the entry/entries. OK closes
the dialog and accepts the choice.
• The optional parameter(s) Text of data type string designate the text above the list box. You can enter
any number of optional parameters of data type string with a maximum length of 45 characters.
Type in the text, which you want to show in the title bar of the dialog, between two vertical bars, for
example (DataList, "|My Company|Text...", "row 2").
Return Value
The return value has the data type list[integer].
When the user clicks Cancel, Plant Simulation returns 0.
Plant Simulation saves the indexes of the selected entries unsorted.
Examples
// A part entering the plant may be processed by more than one machine.
var machPark: list[string]  // You are going to enter the machines that can 
var indices: list[integer]  // process it
machPark.create
machPark[1] := "M7"; machPark[2] := "M12"
machPark[3] := "M4"; machPark[4] := "M19"
indices := promptListN(machPark,
   "Select one or several of the machines that can", "process the part:")
for var i := 1 to Indices.Dim 
   switch indices[i]
   case 1 
   // M7 selected
   case 2 
